ShapeUpgrade_UnifySameDomain: the planarity of each surface is tested once
per merge of faces, not once for each pair of neighbouring faces
(mitcad#235).

IsSameDomain tests both faces' surfaces with GeomLib_IsPlanarSurface,
which samples a B-spline surface at 8 + 3 times its knot spans in each
direction over the whole surface. The faces of a thread that run its 25
turns are split into pieces of a third of a turn sharing their surface;
after a boolean every piece met its tangent neighbours with that test of
the whole surface (40000 points each time), 4 of the 8 s of the face merge
after cutting such a thread.

IntUnifyFaces now keeps the result for each surface it tested (a face
without a location; a located surface is tested as before), so a surface
is sampled once. The results are those of the test itself.

--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeUpgrade/ShapeUpgrade_UnifySameDomain.cxx
